    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0360F3B5A2EC741788B51C99C6E17513/jobs/379599": {
      "title": "Farm Maintenance Specialist",
      "description": "Farm Maintenance Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Farm Maintenance Specialist Hot Job Midway University - Midway, KY 40347 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description Farm Maintenance Specialist Midway University is seeking a motivated, hands-on Farm Maintenance Specialist to help maintain one of Kentucky’s premier collegiate equine facilities. This full-time, hourly position plays a vital role in supporting our Equine Studies program and will focus on the upkeep of pastures, fencing and equipment. Weekend and holiday work will also be required. Examples of work duties, include but are not limited to: Maintain pastures for optimum growth, including mowing, harrowing, seeding, and making recommendations for herbicide and fertilizer application. Operate, maintain, and repair various types of equipment including tractors, mowers, manure spreaders, saws, sprayers and weed eaters. Operate, maintain, and repair light or medium weight trucks. Operate, maintain, and repair tractors and implements used to maintain fields as needed. Light to medium duty carpentry work to repair barns, stalls, equine jumps, etc. Regular maintenance of automatic waterers Work alongside other people within the department and other department personnel in completing assigned tasks Assist the Farm Manager with training students in the operation, maintenance, and repair of farm and facilities Assist the Farm Manager as needed. Qualifications Requirements: High School Diploma or GED required; Bachelor’s preferred. 1-3 years’ prior farm experience required, or equivalent combination of education and experience. The ability to work outdoors, year-round in all types of weather is required.  Commercial chemical applicator’s license or willingness to obtain is required. Prior experience working with horses is preferred. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. At this time, Midway University is unable to provide new employment visa sponsorship. Consideration will be given to candidates who are already authorized to work for any employer in the United States. Midway University is an equal opportunity employer. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
